        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1ef33c06-ffac-582c-8dd4-a92f4106a73e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Griffon Bruxellois, Brussels Griffon, Griffon Belge, Petit Brabançon, English Mastiff, Mastiff\n- Places: Brussels, Belgium\n- Concepts: toy dog breeds, dog breed ancestry, breed traits, canine Chiari-like malformation\n\nFacts:\n- The Griffon Bruxellois, also called the Brussels Griffon, is a toy dog breed named after Brussels in Belgium.\n- The term Griffon Bruxellois may refer to three different breeds: the Griffon Bruxellois, the Griffon Belge, and the Petit Brabançon.\n- The English Mastiff, often called the Mastiff, is an extremely large dog breed that may descend from the ancient Alaunt and Pugnaces Britanniae, with significant input from the Alpine Mastiff in the 19th century.\n- The English Mastiff is distinguished by enormous size, a massive head, a limited range of colours, and a black mask, and it is noted for a gentle and loving nature.\n- Canine Chiari-like malformation is rare in most dog breeds but has reportedly become very widespread in the Cavalier King Charles Spaniel and the Griffon Bruxellois.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
